DTI Secretary Maria Cristina Aldeguer-Roque: na SB Corp is the financial institution where the MSMEs can loan na up to five million po,

asr-002809
02:21:11.120 --> 02:21:14.600
DTI Secretary Maria Cristina Aldeguer-Roque: no collateral, which everybody knows.

asr-002810
02:21:14.600 --> 02:21:17.420
DTI Secretary Maria Cristina Aldeguer-Roque: The small and medium enterprises don't have collateral.

asr-002811
02:21:17.880 --> 02:21:21.720
DTI Secretary Maria Cristina Aldeguer-Roque: And then one year, no payment of principal and interest.

asr-002812
02:21:21.720 --> 02:21:25.479
DTI Secretary Maria Cristina Aldeguer-Roque: So may palugit po sila na makausad ng negosyo nila.

asr-002813
02:21:25.479 --> 02:21:27.920
DTI Secretary Maria Cristina Aldeguer-Roque: Then they can start paying on the second year.

asr-002814
02:21:27.920 --> 02:21:32.120
DTI Secretary Maria Cristina Aldeguer-Roque: So we've introduced newer loan programs.

asr-002815
02:21:32.120 --> 02:21:33.319
Rep. Roberto Nazal: Aside from the P3?

asr-002816
02:21:33.319 --> 02:21:35.240
DTI Secretary Maria Cristina Aldeguer-Roque: Aside from—pardon?

asr-002817
02:21:35.240 --> 02:21:36.700
Rep. Roberto Nazal: Aside from yung P3?

asr-002818
02:21:37.160 --> 02:21:38.660
Rep. Roberto Nazal: Yung Pondo sa Pagbabago?

asr-002821
02:21:38.800 --> 02:21:45.520
DTI Secretary Maria Cristina Aldeguer-Roque: So we have loan programs that were very strategic and specific, especially for the Middle East

asr-002822
02:21:45.520 --> 02:21:46.040
DTI Secretary Maria Cristina Aldeguer-Roque: crisis.

asr-002823
02:21:46.040 --> 02:21:49.720
DTI Secretary Maria Cristina Aldeguer-Roque: And I don't know if you want to hear the loan programs again.

asr-002824
02:21:49.720 --> 02:21:55.600
DTI Secretary Maria Cristina Aldeguer-Roque: So the OFW Negosyo Funds, the Women Enterprise Fund, which we encourage now double income

asr-002825
02:21:55.600 --> 02:21:56.360
DTI Secretary Maria Cristina Aldeguer-Roque: in a family.

asr-002826
02:21:56.760 --> 02:22:01.160
DTI Secretary Maria Cristina Aldeguer-Roque: Kasi we know that pag double income, better education, better quality of life.

asr-002827
02:22:01.160 --> 02:22:06.200
DTI Secretary Maria Cristina Aldeguer-Roque: They can now – the tourism will also go up, then the indirect industries, and then

asr-002828
02:22:06.200 --> 02:22:10.560
DTI Secretary Maria Cristina Aldeguer-Roque: we also have – and our last was the Youth Enterprise Fund.

asr-002829
02:22:10.560 --> 02:22:16.920
DTI Secretary Maria Cristina Aldeguer-Roque: We try to encourage now the youth that are always on the social media to use their time

asr-002830
02:22:16.920 --> 02:22:20.800
DTI Secretary Maria Cristina Aldeguer-Roque: wisely and to start pagnenegosyo at an early age.

asr-002831
02:22:20.800 --> 02:22:25.160
Rep. Roberto Nazal: So in terms of market access, ano po yung programs natin?

asr-002832
02:22:25.160 --> 02:22:25.680
Rep. Roberto Nazal: Uh.

asr-002833
02:22:25.680 --> 02:22:26.020
Rep. Roberto Nazal: Specific programs?

asr-002834
02:22:26.960 --> 02:22:29.960
DTI Secretary Maria Cristina Aldeguer-Roque: We have now different trade shows nationwide.

asr-002835
02:22:29.960 --> 02:22:33.240
DTI Secretary Maria Cristina Aldeguer-Roque: In NCR, we have one to two every month.

asr-002836
02:22:33.240 --> 02:22:37.000
DTI Secretary Maria Cristina Aldeguer-Roque: We also have globally a lot of trade shows.

asr-002837
02:22:37.000 --> 02:22:39.319
DTI Secretary Maria Cristina Aldeguer-Roque: In fact, we've been aggressive now in joining.

asr-002838
02:22:39.319 --> 02:22:40.960
DTI Secretary Maria Cristina Aldeguer-Roque: That's where exports are up.

asr-002839
02:22:40.960 --> 02:22:43.080
DTI Secretary Maria Cristina Aldeguer-Roque: All these trade shows, po, are free.

asr-002840
02:22:43.520 --> 02:22:55.720
DTI Secretary Maria Cristina Aldeguer-Roque: And then we continue to provide also customers from cafes, hotels, different grocery supermarkets.

asr-002841
02:22:55.720 --> 02:22:56.439
DTI Secretary Maria Cristina Aldeguer-Roque: We invite them.

asr-002842
02:22:56.439 --> 02:23:00.800
DTI Secretary Maria Cristina Aldeguer-Roque: Actually, we engage a company that brings in all of these buyers.

asr-002843
02:23:00.800 --> 02:23:08.840
DTI Secretary Maria Cristina Aldeguer-Roque: Then we've also invited companies like Jollibee, companies that are big that can buy from the

asr-002844
02:23:09.520 --> 02:23:11.980
DTI Secretary Maria Cristina Aldeguer-Roque: local manufacturers.

asr-002845
02:23:12.359 --> 02:23:14.960
Rep. Roberto Nazal: How about in terms of accessing the local market?

asr-002846
02:23:14.960 --> 02:23:16.439
DTI Secretary Maria Cristina Aldeguer-Roque: Uh, local, um...

asr-002847
02:23:16.439 --> 02:23:17.760
Rep. Roberto Nazal: Local, let's say, supermarkets?

asr-002848
02:23:17.760 --> 02:23:18.399
DTI Secretary Maria Cristina Aldeguer-Roque: Yes, we do.

asr-002849
02:23:18.399 --> 02:23:25.960
DTI Secretary Maria Cristina Aldeguer-Roque: In fact, SM, Robinsons, Pure Gold, so many of the groceries and supermarkets are also

asr-002850
02:23:25.960 --> 02:23:26.840
DTI Secretary Maria Cristina Aldeguer-Roque: buying from these.

asr-002851
02:23:26.840 --> 02:23:31.000
DTI Secretary Maria Cristina Aldeguer-Roque: And also yung mga cafes, yung mga nagbabottle din, mga caterers.

asr-002861
02:23:31.000 --> 02:23:47.160
Rep. Roberto Nazal: When they buy, are they, hindi ba, pagka meron tayong local retailers, yung ating local retailers, very prohibitive yung pagpasok ng MSMEs para ma-display yung produkto sa kanila.

asr-002862
02:23:47.160 --> 02:23:52.880
Rep. Roberto Nazal: They charge listing fees, they charge kung ano-anong fee na sinisingil na lang sa invoice mo.

asr-002863
02:23:52.880 --> 02:24:00.959
Rep. Roberto Nazal: Kaya minsan, ang nangyayari, yung MSME, sa dami ng sinisingil ng local retailers, pagtingin na lang ang invoice nila, wala na silang kinikita.

asr-002864
02:24:02.000 --> 02:24:11.240
DTI Secretary Maria Cristina Aldeguer-Roque: Okay, let's say for SM, there's a different rate for MSMEs. In fact, they provided in all their malls an area where MSMEs can sell their products.

asr-002865
02:24:11.240 --> 02:24:20.479
DTI Secretary Maria Cristina Aldeguer-Roque: So, mas mababa po yung rent, very much lower. And they also provide different, kasi marami silang supermarkets, groceries.

asr-002866
02:24:20.479 --> 02:24:21.780
Rep. Roberto Nazal: Lalo na for MSMEs?

asr-002867
02:24:22.880 --> 02:24:27.600
DTI Secretary Maria Cristina Aldeguer-Roque: Totally none, kasi they also employ people. So, they need to charge.

asr-002868
02:24:27.600 --> 02:24:40.760
Rep. Roberto Nazal: Pero anong nangyayari po? If you're a local manufacturer, you're an MSME, and then you're, magdi-display kayo sa local retailer,

asr-002869
02:24:40.760 --> 02:24:48.399
Rep. Roberto Nazal: kayo rin, ikaw rin ang nagbabayad ng, what do you call this, yung mga merchandisers.

asr-002870
02:24:48.399 --> 02:24:48.800
Rep. Roberto Nazal: Ah.

asr-002871
02:24:48.800 --> 02:24:52.880
Rep. Roberto Nazal: They do not, kung wala kang merchandiser, you won't be able to display.

asr-002872
02:24:52.880 --> 02:24:55.240
Rep. Roberto Nazal: Display your product, mahuubusan ka sa display.

asr-002873
02:24:55.240 --> 02:25:01.319
DTI Secretary Maria Cristina Aldeguer-Roque: I can talk to them again regarding that, but we've already, we've, in the past, we've established lower rates.

asr-002874
02:25:01.319 --> 02:25:09.120
DTI Secretary Maria Cristina Aldeguer-Roque: But what the others do then, let's say I'm an MSME, I can manufacture for a brand. I'm a subcontractor now.

asr-002875
02:25:09.120 --> 02:25:19.040
DTI Secretary Maria Cristina Aldeguer-Roque: So, at least, kahit papano, I don't pay the listing fees, I don't pay the FDA fees, I don't pay, sure, buy na yung mga produkto ko.

asr-002876
02:25:19.040 --> 02:25:21.720
DTI Secretary Maria Cristina Aldeguer-Roque: So, we encourage them to also be suppliers.

asr-002877
02:25:21.720 --> 02:25:22.080
DTI Secretary Maria Cristina Aldeguer-Roque: Mm-hmm.

asr-002878
02:25:22.080 --> 02:25:23.760
DTI Secretary Maria Cristina Aldeguer-Roque: Rather than to have their own brand.

asr-002879
02:25:23.760 --> 02:25:31.359
DTI Secretary Maria Cristina Aldeguer-Roque: And then, for those that have their own brand, we teach them how to use the social media platform, like, let's say, TikTok, how to sell their product.

asr-002880
02:25:31.359 --> 02:25:36.120
DTI Secretary Maria Cristina Aldeguer-Roque: We've seen a lot of success, ah, through the, example, the Laing, as I've mentioned.

asr-002881
02:25:36.760 --> 02:25:46.240
DTI Secretary Maria Cristina Aldeguer-Roque: They were just a home industry, and then we've introduced the social media platform to them, and they were selling already 300,000 a day.

asr-002882
02:25:46.240 --> 02:25:52.460
DTI Secretary Maria Cristina Aldeguer-Roque: In fact, in the past presidential visit, they were invited by that company, TikTok, itself.

asr-002883
02:25:59.240 --> 02:26:06.840
DTI Secretary Maria Cristina Aldeguer-Roque: So, they can choose if they have the money to pay the listing fees, or they want their own brand, then they can, they have that.

asr-002884
02:26:06.840 --> 02:26:21.600
DTI Secretary Maria Cristina Aldeguer-Roque: Or, if they want, they can also be suppliers, so that they don't have to carry the inventory costs, they don't have to carry also the listing fees, they don't have to carry all the other fees that are needed to be able to showcase their product.

asr-002887
02:26:21.600 --> 02:26:44.640
Rep. Roberto Nazal: Is there a mechanism to control, let's say, um, um, ang ginagawa po ng some retailers, is once lumakas yung produkto ng isang MSME, ah, like in Watson's, for example, gagayahin, and then maglalabas sila ng Watson's brand, and then, tapos, kakainin na yung market nung ano.

asr-002888
02:26:44.640 --> 02:26:50.919
Rep. Roberto Nazal: Kasi, yung tindera nila doon, ang sasabihin, walang available nung sa MSME.

asr-002889
02:26:51.760 --> 02:26:53.840
Rep. Roberto Nazal: Ito nalang Watson's ang bilhin nyo, available.

asr-002890
02:26:54.359 --> 02:26:56.520
DTI Secretary Maria Cristina Aldeguer-Roque: I can check with them regarding that, no?

asr-002891
02:26:56.520 --> 02:27:01.160
DTI Secretary Maria Cristina Aldeguer-Roque: But usually, once you build your brand, kahit papano, there's also the strength in the brand.

asr-002892
02:27:01.160 --> 02:27:04.160
Rep. Roberto Nazal: So, um, let's say other companies...

asr-002893
02:27:04.160 --> 02:27:13.220
Rep. Roberto Nazal: But of course, of course, ma'am, if, if, if the retailer kasi, if they control, uh, we know that most retailers now are controlled by a few companies only.

asr-002894
02:27:13.600 --> 02:27:19.160
Rep. Roberto Nazal: So, they can easily divert the buyer to their, ano...

asr-002895
02:27:19.160 --> 02:27:20.040
DTI Secretary Maria Cristina Aldeguer-Roque: That's possible.

asr-002896
02:27:20.040 --> 02:27:20.200
Rep. Roberto Nazal: Like,

asr-002897
02:27:20.200 --> 02:27:29.639
Rep. Roberto Nazal: One strategy, which I've seen, is that, um, if you have display, alalagay nila, yung display mo, um, walang, walang laman.

asr-002898
02:27:30.439 --> 02:27:32.520
Rep. Roberto Nazal: So, you have to go to the counter to get it.

asr-002899
02:27:34.439 --> 02:27:41.399
Rep. Roberto Nazal: While yung sa kanila is readily available, top shelf, tapos, um, this happens, eh.

asr-002900
02:27:41.399 --> 02:27:43.600
DTI Secretary Maria Cristina Aldeguer-Roque: Yes, actually, Kong, yes, that's possible.

asr-002901
02:27:43.600 --> 02:27:48.940
DTI Secretary Maria Cristina Aldeguer-Roque: So, it's best for the MSMEs not to just have one market or to rely on one market.

asr-002902
02:27:49.080 --> 02:27:49.399
DTI Secretary Maria Cristina Aldeguer-Roque: Yes.

asr-002903
02:27:49.399 --> 02:27:52.120
DTI Secretary Maria Cristina Aldeguer-Roque: They need to be able to use the different platforms.

asr-002904
02:27:52.120 --> 02:27:53.279
DTI Secretary Maria Cristina Aldeguer-Roque: Let's say the e-commerce platform...

asr-002905
02:27:53.279 --> 02:27:53.880
Rep. Roberto Nazal: No, I understand.

asr-002906
02:27:53.880 --> 02:28:03.340
Rep. Roberto Nazal: All I'm just saying is that, syempre, DTI has to protect MSMEs in terms of policy para mawala naman yung mga predatory practices.

asr-002907
02:28:03.680 --> 02:28:04.640
DTI Secretary Maria Cristina Aldeguer-Roque: Yes, we can...

asr-002908
02:28:04.640 --> 02:28:09.040
DTI Secretary Maria Cristina Aldeguer-Roque: I can talk to the different establishments regarding this, um, practice.

asr-002909
02:28:09.040 --> 02:28:12.440
Rep. Roberto Nazal: So, I'd like to go to, um, SB Corp.

asr-002910
02:28:13.520 --> 02:28:20.320
Rep. Roberto Nazal: Before we give SB Corp another 840.17 million for P3 in 2027,

asr-002911
02:28:21.680 --> 02:28:22.319
Rep. Roberto Nazal: can you give us...

asr-002912
02:28:22.319 --> 02:28:27.539
Rep. Roberto Nazal: Can you give us one consolidated accounting of all government funds entrusted to SB Corp since P3 began?

asr-002913
02:28:28.439 --> 02:28:31.679
DTI Secretary Maria Cristina Aldeguer-Roque: Um, I'll defer to, um, President Bobby of SB Corp.

asr-002914
02:28:32.720 --> 02:28:33.200
DTI Secretary Maria Cristina Aldeguer-Roque: Ah, okay.

asr-002915
02:28:36.479 --> 02:28:39.760
DTI Secretary Maria Cristina Aldeguer-Roque: Ah, wala si President Bobby, so go ahead, introduce yourself.

asr-002916
02:28:39.760 --> 02:28:40.680
SB Corp respondent (functional attribution; exact individual not established): Thank you, Sec.

asr-002917
02:28:40.680 --> 02:28:41.599
SB Corp respondent (functional attribution; exact individual not established): Ah, thank you, Madam Chair.

asr-002918
02:28:42.359 --> 02:28:45.680
SB Corp respondent (functional attribution; exact individual not established): Ah, with regards to, ah, the question, Madam Chair,

asr-002919
02:28:46.120 --> 02:28:51.780
SB Corp respondent (functional attribution; exact individual not established): ah, SB Corp started receiving, ah, annual allocations under the GAA.

asr-002920
02:28:52.359 --> 02:28:54.420
SB Corp respondent (functional attribution; exact individual not established): Ah, beginning 2017.

asr-002921
02:28:55.240 --> 02:29:01.280
SB Corp respondent (functional attribution; exact individual not established): So, more or less, ah, we've received around, ah, 10 billion pesos since 2017.

asr-002922
02:29:01.800 --> 02:29:06.340
SB Corp respondent (functional attribution; exact individual not established): And that includes the 1 billion peso that we received for 2026.

asr-002923
02:29:07.080 --> 02:29:16.000
SB Corp respondent (functional attribution; exact individual not established): So, for the, ah, 10 billion pesos, what we have actually released our loans are, ah, more than threefold.

asr-002924
02:29:16.000 --> 02:29:17.840
SB Corp respondent (functional attribution; exact individual not established): Probably we've released 30 billion.

asr-002925
02:29:17.840 --> 02:29:21.240
SB Corp respondent (functional attribution; exact individual not established): So, ah, what this means is that what we've lent out,

asr-002926
02:29:21.240 --> 02:29:21.920
SB Corp respondent (functional attribution; exact individual not established): we've collected through...

asr-002927
02:29:21.920 --> 02:29:22.679
SB Corp respondent (functional attribution; exact individual not established): Through the years.

asr-002928
02:29:23.160 --> 02:29:26.439
SB Corp respondent (functional attribution; exact individual not established): And now, ah, we still have the money at SB Corp.

asr-002929
02:29:26.439 --> 02:29:34.080
SB Corp respondent (functional attribution; exact individual not established): So, actually, the total loan portfolio under the P3 program amounts roughly, ah, around 10 billion as well.

asr-002930
02:29:34.840 --> 02:29:39.120
Rep. Roberto Nazal: How many, um, beneficiaries have you lent out to?

asr-002931
02:29:39.120 --> 02:29:43.660
SB Corp respondent (functional attribution; exact individual not established): Siguro po, ah, through both, ah, direct, ah, retail and wholesale,

asr-002932
02:29:44.359 --> 02:29:49.200
SB Corp respondent (functional attribution; exact individual not established): ah, more than 500,000 na po ang ating mga natulungan under the P3 program, Madam Chair.

asr-002933
02:29:50.324 --> 02:29:51.512
Rep. Roberto Nazal: Ah, I'd just like to...

asr-002934
02:29:51.720 --> 02:29:53.000
Rep. Roberto Nazal: in the interest of time,

asr-002935
02:29:53.000 --> 02:29:54.080
Rep. Roberto Nazal: magre-request na lang ako

asr-002936
02:29:54.080 --> 02:29:57.920
Rep. Roberto Nazal: ng list, um, of borrowers and how much was released.

asr-002937
02:30:01.160 --> 02:30:02.980
SB Corp respondent (functional attribution; exact individual not established): We'll provide that, Madam Chair.

asr-002938
02:30:05.240 --> 02:30:10.980
Rep. Roberto Nazal: So the 2026 subsidy for P3 was 1 billion, as you mentioned.

asr-002939
02:30:11.120 --> 02:30:17.700
Rep. Roberto Nazal: SB Corp's report shows the full amount obligated and disbursed by June 30, 2026.

asr-002940
02:30:18.399 --> 02:30:27.100
Rep. Roberto Nazal: Yet physical accomplishment was only around 19,373 beneficiaries against a 40,000 annual target.

asr-002941
02:30:27.760 --> 02:30:34.619
Rep. Roberto Nazal: When SB Corp reports to Congress that 1 billion has been 100% disbursed, what does disbursed mean?

asr-002942
02:30:35.399 --> 02:30:40.760
Rep. Roberto Nazal: Does it mean actually na umabot po sa 40,000 micro-entrepreneurs?

asr-002943
02:30:40.760 --> 02:30:44.140
Rep. Roberto Nazal: Or does it mean SB Corp transferred it to a conduit?

asr-002944
02:30:44.960 --> 02:30:48.619
Rep. Charisse Anne C. Hernandez: Thank you, Representative Nazal. That will be your last question.

asr-002945
02:30:52.520 --> 02:30:56.880
SB Corp respondent (functional attribution; exact individual not established): Yes, to reply, Madam Chair, with regards to disbursed,

asr-002946
02:30:56.880 --> 02:30:58.479
SB Corp respondent (functional attribution; exact individual not established): what it means is that we've actually,

asr-002947
02:30:58.479 --> 02:31:07.400
SB Corp respondent (functional attribution; exact individual not established): we've actually released the loans either through our wholesale conduits or either through our direct retail borrowers.

asr-002948
02:31:07.920 --> 02:31:18.300
SB Corp respondent (functional attribution; exact individual not established): With regards to the P3 loan portfolio distribution, it's roughly 55% direct retail and 45% wholesale.

asr-002949
02:31:18.720 --> 02:31:23.160
SB Corp respondent (functional attribution; exact individual not established): So mas marami na po ang nabibigay natin through direct retail, Madam Chair.

asr-002950
02:31:27.439 --> 02:31:31.920
Rep. Roberto Nazal: Hingi na lang po ako ng listahan nung what has actually reached and borrowed.

asr-002951
02:31:31.920 --> 02:31:43.080
Rep. Roberto Nazal: Kasi ito sa mga borrower remains outstanding, has been collected and revolved, is past due, is non-performing, has been written off, and remains as cash or investments with SB Corp or a conduit.

asr-002952
02:31:43.080 --> 02:31:44.000
SB Corp respondent (functional attribution; exact individual not established): We'll provide, Madam Chair.

asr-002953
02:31:45.160 --> 02:31:53.560
Rep. Roberto Nazal: My last question is, why do taxpayers subsidize the capital but borrowers can still pay up to 30% annually?

asr-002954
02:31:54.080 --> 02:32:00.200
Rep. Roberto Nazal: Kasi di ba, P3 is supposed to be to rescue micro-entrepreneurs from 5-6 lenders.

asr-002957
02:32:00.760 --> 02:32:07.400
Rep. Roberto Nazal: But the program permits an all-in rate of up to 2.5% monthly or around 30% annually.

asr-002958
02:32:08.319 --> 02:32:16.319
Rep. Roberto Nazal: So if taxpayers are providing the capital, why should the poorest micro-entrepreneurs still pay as much as 30% per year?

asr-002959
02:32:16.319 --> 02:32:17.920
Rep. Roberto Nazal: Hindi po ba natin puwedeng ibaba iyon?

asr-002960
02:32:20.800 --> 02:32:21.920
Rep. Charisse Anne C. Hernandez: Okay. Thank you, Representative Nazal.

asr-002961
02:32:21.920 --> 02:32:22.859
Rep. Roberto Nazal: Yes, Madam Chair.

asr-002962
02:32:24.279 --> 02:32:30.279
Rep. Roberto Nazal: Just to add to that, what is the actual weighted average effective rate being paid by P3 borrowers?

asr-002963
02:32:30.279 --> 02:32:33.360
Rep. Roberto Nazal: Including interest, service charges, processing fees, insurance.

asr-002964
02:32:33.840 --> 02:32:36.260
Rep. Roberto Nazal: Compounding deposits and every other charge.

asr-002965
02:32:37.960 --> 02:32:45.240
Rep. Roberto Nazal: Tapos, how much does SB Corp charge its conduits and how much does the conduit add before the money reaches the borrower?

asr-002966
02:32:45.240 --> 02:32:46.920
Rep. Charisse Anne C. Hernandez: All right, compounding question.

asr-002967
02:32:46.920 --> 02:32:48.080
Rep. Charisse Anne C. Hernandez: Okay, sir.

asr-002968
02:32:48.080 --> 02:32:49.240
Rep. Charisse Anne C. Hernandez: Thank you, Representative Nazal.

asr-002969
02:32:51.000 --> 02:32:54.668
DTI Secretary Maria Cristina Aldeguer-Roque: Honorable Kong, we will meet again regarding that.

asr-002970
02:32:54.954 --> 02:32:58.880
DTI Secretary Maria Cristina Aldeguer-Roque: We'll discuss it with the board and then we will present it to you.

asr-002971
02:32:58.880 --> 02:33:02.840
DTI Secretary Maria Cristina Aldeguer-Roque: So all your concerns, po, we can write it down.

asr-002972
02:33:02.840 --> 02:33:04.080
DTI Secretary Maria Cristina Aldeguer-Roque: And then we can...

asr-002973
02:33:04.080 --> 02:33:07.760
DTI Secretary Maria Cristina Aldeguer-Roque: Make some changes if there is a need to make some changes.

asr-002974
02:33:07.760 --> 02:33:13.720
DTI Secretary Maria Cristina Aldeguer-Roque: Kasi like with SB Corp before, in the past, they also required collateral.

asr-002975
02:33:13.720 --> 02:33:16.439
DTI Secretary Maria Cristina Aldeguer-Roque: But now up to 5 million, wala na pong collateral.

asr-002976
02:33:16.439 --> 02:33:27.760
DTI Secretary Maria Cristina Aldeguer-Roque: So as time goes by, there are some things that we may need to amend or we may need to change that will be good or will be best for the people also.

asr-002977
02:33:29.120 --> 02:33:29.359
