05:23:16.558 --> 05:23:18.320
DTI Undersecretary Ceferino S. Rodolfo: So, yun pong isang possible, LNG.

asr-006127
05:23:18.920 --> 05:23:19.260
Rep. Antonio L. Tinio: Okay.

asr-006128
05:23:19.878 --> 05:23:22.680
Rep. Antonio L. Tinio: Meron silang sariling exclusively for them.

asr-006129
05:23:23.320 --> 05:23:23.878
Rep. Antonio L. Tinio: Parang ganon.

asr-006130
05:23:25.360 --> 05:23:30.198
DTI Undersecretary Ceferino S. Rodolfo: It will be under the Department of Energy and ERC regulations.

asr-006131
05:23:30.558 --> 05:23:34.218
DTI Undersecretary Ceferino S. Rodolfo: Kaya ko lang po sinasabi ito, kasi possibly ho na exclusive for them.

asr-006132
05:23:35.160 --> 05:23:38.580
DTI Undersecretary Ceferino S. Rodolfo: Pag nagbenta ho sila sa labas, kailangan po nila ng permit.

asr-006133
05:23:39.280 --> 05:23:41.020
DTI Undersecretary Ceferino S. Rodolfo: So, it will be under Philippine laws.

asr-006134
05:23:41.920 --> 05:23:43.400
Rep. Antonio L. Tinio: So, pwede rin magbenta na labas.

asr-006135
05:23:43.400 --> 05:23:45.480
Rep. Antonio L. Tinio: How about water? Ano yung nakikita nyo?

asr-006136
05:23:46.878 --> 05:23:50.580
DTI Undersecretary Ceferino S. Rodolfo: Dalawa po yung tinatahak pagdating po sa water.

asr-006137
05:23:51.200 --> 05:23:58.880
DTI Undersecretary Ceferino S. Rodolfo: One is yung nabanggit na rin po ni BCDA President Jake Binkang, yung pong harvesting of the surface water.

asr-006138
05:24:00.080 --> 05:24:08.440
DTI Undersecretary Ceferino S. Rodolfo: Kitang-kitaw natin ngayon mga nag-uulan itong past two weeks, yung mga rivers rumaragasa, nasasayang po yung tubig.

asr-006139
05:24:08.440 --> 05:24:13.600
DTI Undersecretary Ceferino S. Rodolfo: So, yung possibility po of having an impounding station to harvest this water.

asr-006140
05:24:13.600 --> 05:24:15.038
DTI Undersecretary Ceferino S. Rodolfo: Yung pangalawa po na...

asr-006141
05:24:15.840 --> 05:24:24.400
DTI Undersecretary Ceferino S. Rodolfo: Yung nakikita po natin would be a desalination facility in Subic, tapos so ipapipe papunta sa Clark.

asr-006142
05:24:25.718 --> 05:24:33.400
Rep. Antonio L. Tinio: Okay. So, rainwater, parang ganun, isa? Rainwater?

asr-006143
05:24:33.400 --> 05:24:35.680
Rep. Antonio L. Tinio: Of course, isang buong ecosystem to, no?

asr-006144
05:24:35.680 --> 05:24:46.360
Rep. Antonio L. Tinio: So, pag kinuha't ginamit nila yan, yung tubig na yon hindi necessarily magagamit sa irigasyon or bilang inumin.

asr-006145
05:24:47.120 --> 05:24:47.558
Rep. Antonio L. Tinio: So...

asr-006146
05:24:47.558 --> 05:24:49.260
Rep. Antonio L. Tinio: Kasama rin yon, di ba?

asr-006147
05:24:49.280 --> 05:24:49.580
Rep. Antonio L. Tinio: Okay.

asr-006148
05:24:50.680 --> 05:24:51.398
Rep. Antonio L. Tinio: At kung...

asr-006149
05:24:51.840 --> 05:24:58.840
Rep. Antonio L. Tinio: Of course, it's well known that water used for cooling data centers, eh hindi lang tubig yon.

asr-006150
05:24:58.840 --> 05:25:00.440
Rep. Antonio L. Tinio: May mga coal land, may mga kemikal.

asr-006151
05:25:00.440 --> 05:25:03.958
Rep. Antonio L. Tinio: Kaya yun yung isang concern, nagiging madumi yung tubig.

asr-006152
05:25:03.958 --> 05:25:04.480
Rep. Antonio L. Tinio: Tama po?

asr-006153
05:25:05.760 --> 05:25:07.160
DTI Undersecretary Ceferino S. Rodolfo: Kasama po, Madam Chair.

asr-006154
05:25:07.160 --> 05:25:11.180
DTI Undersecretary Ceferino S. Rodolfo: Kasama po sa requirement ng BCDA.

asr-006155
05:25:11.280 --> 05:25:12.440
DTI Undersecretary Ceferino S. Rodolfo: Or kung saan po

asr-006156
05:25:12.440 --> 05:25:12.680
DTI Undersecretary Ceferino S. Rodolfo: Hindi...

asr-006157
05:25:13.638 --> 05:25:17.520
DTI Undersecretary Ceferino S. Rodolfo: Kahit tunga limbawa, whether it's a manufacturing facility or...

asr-006158
05:25:17.520 --> 05:25:22.820
DTI Undersecretary Ceferino S. Rodolfo: Kung ano man, would be full compliance with our environmental compliance.

asr-006159
05:25:23.040 --> 05:25:25.840
DTI Undersecretary Ceferino S. Rodolfo: With our ECC, it's all of the environmental laws.

asr-006160
05:25:25.840 --> 05:25:29.220
DTI Undersecretary Ceferino S. Rodolfo: Kasama na rin po yung water treatment facilities.

asr-006161
05:25:29.920 --> 05:25:32.718
Rep. Antonio L. Tinio: Nabanggit nyo na hindi lang Paxilica.

asr-006162
05:25:32.718 --> 05:25:43.238
Rep. Antonio L. Tinio: Alam pa yung ibang areas na magkakaroon, posibleng magkaroon, tinatarget na magkaroon ng mga Paxilica-related projects outside of New Clark City?

asr-006163
05:25:44.360 --> 05:25:46.160
DTI Undersecretary Ceferino S. Rodolfo: Madam Chair, eto po ay...

asr-006164
05:25:46.160 --> 05:25:53.280
DTI Undersecretary Ceferino S. Rodolfo: Lahat po ng itong mga discussions dito are all based on Philippine internal discussions.

asr-006165
05:25:53.760 --> 05:25:55.080
DTI Undersecretary Ceferino S. Rodolfo: So tinitignan po natin.

asr-006166
05:25:55.080 --> 05:26:05.080
DTI Undersecretary Ceferino S. Rodolfo: Dahil bago naman kung magkaroon ng Paxilica, bago tayo sumama dun sa statement on the Paxilica, talagang pinopromote na po natin.

asr-006167
05:26:05.080 --> 05:26:09.378
DTI Undersecretary Ceferino S. Rodolfo: Sinasabi natin for the next two and a half years of this administration.

asr-006168
05:26:09.440 --> 05:26:15.180
DTI Undersecretary Ceferino S. Rodolfo: Noon po, ang sinasabi natin, we will be focusing on mining and mineral processing.

asr-006169
05:26:15.760 --> 05:26:18.100
DTI Undersecretary Ceferino S. Rodolfo: Number two, on digital infrastructure.

asr-006170
05:26:18.558 --> 05:26:23.300
DTI Undersecretary Ceferino S. Rodolfo: Number three, on advanced manufacturing, including on semiconductors and electronics.

asr-006171
05:26:23.680 --> 05:26:25.560
DTI Undersecretary Ceferino S. Rodolfo: And then number three, on tourism.

asr-006172
05:26:26.160 --> 05:26:28.040
DTI Undersecretary Ceferino S. Rodolfo: So yung pong tatlong mga...

asr-006173
05:26:28.798 --> 05:26:36.980
DTI Undersecretary Ceferino S. Rodolfo: Ang relevant po dito sa Paxilica are mining and mineral processing, and then yung advanced manufacturing, and then yung digital infrastructure.

asr-006174
05:26:37.480 --> 05:26:45.760
DTI Undersecretary Ceferino S. Rodolfo: So lahat po, may mga internal discussions tayo, tinitignan natin, saan ba pinaka-appropriate sa mga lugar dito sa Pilipinas, yung mga yun.

asr-006175
05:26:45.760 --> 05:26:56.158
DTI Undersecretary Ceferino S. Rodolfo: So for example po, si Department of ICT, meron po siyang ginawa na AI infrastructure roadmap.

asr-006176
05:26:57.040 --> 05:27:10.078
DTI Undersecretary Ceferino S. Rodolfo: So dun po, na-identify niya kung saan yung mga posibling lugar, for example, for data centers, kung saan meron kang tubig, at saka kung saan meron kang power.

asr-006177
05:27:11.798 --> 05:27:17.000
DTI Undersecretary Ceferino S. Rodolfo: So naging controversial recently yung sa Oton, sa Iloilo ba yun?

asr-006178
05:27:17.000 --> 05:27:17.520
DTI Undersecretary Ceferino S. Rodolfo: Kasama ba iyon?

asr-006179
05:27:17.520 --> 05:27:26.878
DTI Undersecretary Ceferino S. Rodolfo: Hindi po siya kasama, nor has that investor coordinated with the Board of Investments.

asr-006180
05:27:26.878 --> 05:27:29.840
Rep. Antonio L. Tinio: Okay. Chair, marami pang mga concerns regarding this.

asr-006181
05:27:29.840 --> 05:27:42.800
Rep. Antonio L. Tinio: Actually, ang suggestion ko po ay dapat magbigay ng hiwalay at specific briefing ang Department on this Paxilica, kasi nga, napaka-controversyal na usapin, Chair.

asr-006182
05:27:43.360 --> 05:27:45.100
Rep. Antonio L. Tinio: Okay ba yun, Chair? Anong tingin nyo?

asr-006183
05:27:46.320 --> 05:27:47.558
Rep. Charisse Anne C. Hernandez: Yes, Kong. I think...

asr-006184
05:27:47.558 --> 05:27:54.500
Rep. Charisse Anne C. Hernandez: We need further discussions. And of course, as Dave mentioned, they're very open naman po with this discussion.

asr-006185
05:27:55.558 --> 05:27:57.820
Rep. Charisse Anne C. Hernandez: Now, lipat lang po tayo sa ibang concerns.

asr-006186
05:27:58.360 --> 05:28:04.000
Rep. Antonio L. Tinio: Una muna yung kaugnay po sa CARS. Kanina, may nabanggit si Sec na nabayaran na raw yung...

asr-006187
05:28:05.080 --> 05:28:09.520
Rep. Antonio L. Tinio: You mentioned that. Nabayaran na yung... What were your words?

asr-006188
05:28:15.280 --> 05:28:18.280
Rep. Antonio L. Tinio: We're getting the budget from the DBM for this.

asr-006189
05:28:19.558 --> 05:28:21.120
Rep. Antonio L. Tinio: This is with regard to...

asr-006190
05:28:21.120 --> 05:28:24.140
Rep. Antonio L. Tinio: Is it the race? Or CARS?

asr-006191
05:28:24.798 --> 05:28:31.900
DTI Secretary Maria Cristina Aldeguer-Roque: Yes, Honorable Kong. This is from the CARS program, yung incentives na for Toyota and for Mitsubishi.

asr-006192
05:28:31.920 --> 05:28:39.938
Rep. Antonio L. Tinio: Okay. Ngayon, ang tanong ko, you're getting the budget to DBM when, as far as I know, the appropriations for that,

asr-006193
05:28:41.000 --> 05:28:47.440
Rep. Antonio L. Tinio: originally nasa budget proposal nyo, napunta sa unprogrammed appropriations, and it was vetoed by the President. Tama?

asr-006194
05:28:47.440 --> 05:28:48.040
DTI Secretary Maria Cristina Aldeguer-Roque: Yes. Tama.

asr-006195
05:28:48.040 --> 05:28:55.220
Rep. Antonio L. Tinio: So, iyon iyong 200 [unclear], 300 [unclear] million.

asr-006196
05:28:56.280 --> 05:29:00.878
Rep. Antonio L. Tinio: So, na-intriga ako sa statement nyo that you are getting the budget from the DBM.

asr-006197
05:29:00.878 --> 05:29:06.958
Rep. Antonio L. Tinio: Paano nyo makukuha yung budget when nasa unprogrammed nga, tapos dinito pa?

asr-006198
05:29:07.958 --> 05:29:15.000
DTI Secretary Maria Cristina Aldeguer-Roque: Yes, actually, from the DPWH ito. Yusek Perry can explain it further.

asr-006199
05:29:15.000 --> 05:29:19.160
Rep. Antonio L. Tinio: Sa DPWH? Okay, please explain. Intriga ako lalo.

asr-006200
05:29:19.160 --> 05:29:21.520
Rep. Charisse Anne C. Hernandez: Go ahead, Yusek Perry.

asr-006201
05:29:21.520 --> 05:29:25.180
DTI Undersecretary Ceferino S. Rodolfo: Madam Chair, thank you for the question, Representative Tinio.

asr-006202
05:29:25.718 --> 05:29:30.760
DTI Undersecretary Ceferino S. Rodolfo: So, yung total amount po is 5.1 billion pesos.

asr-006203
05:29:30.760 --> 05:29:44.100
DTI Undersecretary Ceferino S. Rodolfo: Ito po yung utang natin kay Toyota, Mitsubishi, Denso, Manly Plastics, Valery, F-Tech Philippines, SMRC Automotive Technology, Roberts Automotive, tsaka...

asr-006204
05:29:44.840 --> 05:29:55.118
DTI Undersecretary Ceferino S. Rodolfo: So both the program participants at the model level, so yun pong mga banyaga, pati rin po yung mga local na mga nagsusupply ng mga auto parts.

asr-006205
05:29:55.558 --> 05:30:14.600
DTI Undersecretary Ceferino S. Rodolfo: So ang total amount po ng arirages natin, ang utang natin is 5.156 billion pesos. Tama po kayo na una po meron kaming 125 million pesos yata na nasa budget namin tapos nilagay sa unprogrammed allocation na Vito po.

asr-006206
05:30:14.600 --> 05:30:25.240
DTI Undersecretary Ceferino S. Rodolfo: Tapos ngayon dahil sa kailangan talagang pagkakautang na po natin ito, so kailangan talagang bayaran dahil nag-deliver na po sila ng kanilang mga commitments.

asr-006207
05:30:25.240 --> 05:30:52.080
DTI Undersecretary Ceferino S. Rodolfo: So kukunin po yun, na-identify po. Pwede po kasi mag-identify ka ng savings from other government agencies. Ang nakita po ay may savings po si DPWH. Tapos so yun po yung pagkukuha na ng 5.1 billion pesos. Yung naging savings po nila for 2020-2025.

asr-006208
05:30:52.080 --> 05:30:54.578
DTI Undersecretary Ceferino S. Rodolfo: So savings of 5 billion.

asr-006209
05:30:55.520 --> 05:31:11.200
DTI Undersecretary Ceferino S. Rodolfo: 5.1 billion from DPWH 2025, yun ang gagamitin na pambayad sa CARS. So augmentation from savings essentially. Provided may item para doon. Meron bang item para doon?

asr-006210
05:31:11.200 --> 05:31:25.440
DTI Undersecretary Ceferino S. Rodolfo: Meron pa rin po item na nakalagay doon sa GAAN natin. Meron po kasing meron tayong nakalagay doon na parang maliit lang po na implementation of the CARS program. I think 10 million pesos.

asr-006211
05:31:25.440 --> 05:31:30.278
DTI Undersecretary Ceferino S. Rodolfo: So may paglalagyan pa rin kung kung baga na bahay. May bahay na tinatawag. May bahay po tayo na paglalagyan.

asr-006212
05:31:30.638 --> 05:31:37.780
Rep. Antonio L. Tinio: Okay. Pero ito pala ang nakaka, ngayon ko lang nalaman, savings may 5 billion. Ah, okay.

asr-006213
05:31:38.638 --> 05:31:39.040
DTI Undersecretary Ceferino S. Rodolfo: Sorry po.

asr-006214
05:31:39.040 --> 05:31:39.958
Rep. Antonio L. Tinio: Baka, sige baka.

asr-006215
05:31:39.958 --> 05:31:47.718
DTI Undersecretary Ceferino S. Rodolfo: Just to correct, Madam Chair, 4.081 billion po pala yun.

asr-006216
05:31:47.718 --> 05:31:53.780
DTI Undersecretary Ceferino S. Rodolfo: 4.081 billion savings tapos ngayon ipambabayad sa Toyota, sa Mitsubishi.

asr-006217
05:31:54.280 --> 05:31:55.080
DTI Undersecretary Ceferino S. Rodolfo: [unclear],

asr-006218
05:31:55.080 --> 05:31:57.120
DTI Undersecretary Ceferino S. Rodolfo: And others.

asr-006219
05:31:57.120 --> 05:31:59.120
DTI Undersecretary Ceferino S. Rodolfo: para sa mga incentives nila.

asr-006219-split-2
05:31:59.120 --> 05:32:05.718
Rep. Antonio L. Tinio: Okay. So thank you for that clarification. Magtatanong din tayo sa DBM at sa DPWH regarding this, no?

asr-006220
05:32:05.718 --> 05:32:24.320
Rep. Antonio L. Tinio: Okay. Yung third na lang na concern natin with regard to the tariffs imposed by the US, yung 12.5% dahil daw nag, the Philippines imports from countries with forced labor.

asr-006221
05:32:25.638 --> 05:32:35.840
Rep. Antonio L. Tinio: At ang sabi ng DTI, as far as I know, mga 40%, up to 40% ng Philippine exports affected dito. Tama po ba?

asr-006222
05:32:35.840 --> 05:32:55.080
Rep. Antonio L. Tinio: Could you elaborate? Bakit tayo, akala ko ba magkaibigan ang Pilipinas at US pero pinatawan ng 12.5%? Yung Malaysia, Indonesia, parang 10% lang yata? Diba? Tayo 12 pa?

asr-006223
05:32:55.080 --> 05:33:05.400
Rep. Antonio L. Tinio: 12.5. Please explain the consequences, anong epekto sa mga exporters natin? Sino-sino ang mga ito at anong ginagawa nyo?

asr-006224
05:33:06.440 --> 05:33:13.140
Rep. Antonio L. Tinio: Dahil syempre, dihado, magiging mas mahal ang mga produktong Pilipino in highly competitive export markets.

asr-006225
05:33:13.440 --> 05:33:23.200
DTI Secretary Maria Cristina Aldeguer-Roque: Yes, actually, Kong, for the exporters, we also try to find, in case may problem sila pagpasok ng goods sa US, we find other markets for them.

asr-006226
05:33:23.200 --> 05:33:42.080
DTI Secretary Maria Cristina Aldeguer-Roque: We have different foreign trade attachés globally. So, nakakahanap po kami ng market para sa kanila and also locally. I'll forward you, Kong, Honorable Kong, to the trade negotiator, to our chief negotiator to discuss yung 12.5%.

asr-006227
05:33:42.080 --> 05:33:44.360
DTI Secretary Maria Cristina Aldeguer-Roque: Usec. Allan?

asr-006228
05:33:44.360 --> 05:33:51.520
Rep. Antonio L. Tinio: Ano ba na-explain nyo? Bakit, ano yung sabihin nito? Like, my understanding, mainly this is...

asr-006229
05:33:52.920 --> 05:34:03.900
Rep. Antonio L. Tinio: meant to penalize countries that import from China, among others. Diba ganun? O, huwag na tayo maglokohan. Yun yun eh. Sige, please.

asr-006230
05:34:05.638 --> 05:34:23.120
DTI Undersecretary Allan B. Gepty: Thank you, ma'am, and good afternoon, Your Honors. Number one, with respect to the imposition of tariffs by the United States, I think in terms of context, Po, Your Honor, we have to understand that when President Trump,

asr-006231
05:34:23.120 --> 05:34:47.160
DTI Undersecretary Allan B. Gepty: assumed office, the policy of the United States has been to impose unilateral tariffs. So, basically, the direction is really for them to hit countries wherein they have deficit. But, of course, the first unilateral tariffs was declared unconstitutional by the US Supreme Court, and so they resorted again to another basis by which they can impose unilateral tariffs.

asr-006232
05:34:47.558 --> 05:34:53.418
DTI Undersecretary Allan B. Gepty: After that, they imposed Section 122 tariffs, which can only last for 150 days.

asr-006233
05:34:53.878 --> 05:35:13.980
DTI Undersecretary Allan B. Gepty: And then, after the expiration of Section 1 to 2, now they initiated the investigation under Section 301, and that's the basis by which they have imposed the 12.5% tariffs for, I think, 67 countries, including the Philippines, and for, I think, only around 10 countries, 10%.

asr-006234
05:35:15.200 --> 05:35:22.780
DTI Undersecretary Allan B. Gepty: Now, the basis of Section 301 tariffs under the Trade Regulation Act of the United States, Your Honor, is actually...

asr-006235
05:35:23.558 --> 05:35:38.760
DTI Undersecretary Allan B. Gepty: premise on the fact that countries or economies trading with the United States has no law that bans or prohibits the importation of goods which are made or results of forced labor.

asr-006236
05:35:39.600 --> 05:35:52.058
DTI Undersecretary Allan B. Gepty: So, that's the basis. So, in other words, it doesn't mean that a particular country or economy has a weak regime when it comes to combating, for example, forced labor.

asr-006237
05:35:52.878 --> 05:36:07.460
DTI Undersecretary Allan B. Gepty: So, in the case of the Philippines, we issued a joint administrative order institutionalizing the mechanism by which we can address that particular concern of the United States.

asr-006238
05:36:07.958 --> 05:36:17.558
DTI Undersecretary Allan B. Gepty: And the same is under evaluation now of the US for purposes of at least compliance to their Section 301 investigation.

asr-006239
05:36:18.120 --> 05:36:19.740
DTI Undersecretary Allan B. Gepty: So, iyon po ngayon iyong status ngayon.

asr-006240
05:36:20.680 --> 05:36:22.440
DTI Undersecretary Allan B. Gepty: Negotiations are still ongoing.

asr-006241
05:36:23.120 --> 05:36:26.600
DTI Undersecretary Allan B. Gepty: In fact, itong recent issuance po ng JAO, under evaluation.

asr-006242
05:36:26.600 --> 05:36:38.958
DTI Undersecretary Allan B. Gepty: But we have highlighted the fact that the Philippines has a strong legal regime as far as addressing forced labor from the Constitution, laws, rules and regulations, among others po.

asr-006243
05:36:38.958 --> 05:36:41.180
DTI Undersecretary Allan B. Gepty: So, yan po yung naging basihan po nun.

asr-006244
05:36:42.558 --> 05:36:45.360
Rep. Antonio L. Tinio: So, Chair, just to tatapusin natin.

asr-006245
05:36:45.360 --> 05:36:46.920
Rep. Charisse Anne C. Hernandez: Wind down po with your question.

asr-006246
05:36:46.920 --> 05:36:52.578
Rep. Antonio L. Tinio: So, una, kailangan magpasa natin tayo ng bagong batas para...

asr-006247
05:36:55.320 --> 05:36:57.160
Rep. Antonio L. Tinio: lift, maalis tayo sa listahan, parang ganun ba?

asr-006248
05:36:57.958 --> 05:37:12.440
Rep. Antonio L. Tinio: Pangalawa, meron ba tayong kakayahan para ma-determine whether or not imports into the Philippines were produced with forced labor?

asr-006249
05:37:12.440 --> 05:37:14.158
Rep. Antonio L. Tinio: O, kaya, paano gagawin yun?

asr-006250
05:37:15.400 --> 05:37:22.920
Rep. Antonio L. Tinio: At pangatlo, pwede po bang mabigyan tayo ng listahan ng mga apektadong industriya?

asr-006251
05:37:22.920 --> 05:37:31.480
Rep. Antonio L. Tinio: Yung sinabi ni yung Secretary na meron ng mga hindi na maka-import sa US, kaya tutulungan daw ng DTI, humanap ng ibang markets.

asr-006252
05:37:31.480 --> 05:37:33.120
Rep. Antonio L. Tinio: Which industries in particular?

asr-006253
05:37:33.120 --> 05:37:34.558
Rep. Antonio L. Tinio: Kasi may mga exemptions din, di ba?

asr-006254
05:37:34.558 --> 05:37:41.558
Rep. Antonio L. Tinio: Yung mga automotive, I think semiconductors, ganun, hindi sinama eh, di ba?

asr-006255
05:37:41.558 --> 05:37:42.680
Rep. Antonio L. Tinio: So, which in particular?

asr-006256
05:37:42.680 --> 05:37:45.138
Rep. Antonio L. Tinio: My understanding, it's like garments and so on.

asr-006257
05:37:46.200 --> 05:37:48.180
Rep. Antonio L. Tinio: Pwede po ba mabigyan ng...

asr-006258
05:37:48.200 --> 05:37:52.740
Rep. Antonio L. Tinio: Para malaman natin, sino yung mga natamaan na...

asr-006259
05:37:52.840 --> 05:37:54.380
Rep. Antonio L. Tinio: ...exporters na Pilipino?

asr-006260
05:37:54.920 --> 05:38:00.520
DTI Secretary Maria Cristina Aldeguer-Roque: Yes, Honorable Kong, I'll forward you to EMB, Bianca, Export Marketing Bureau.

